# Conformance probe pack for ruling 24 of spec 0.15 on the `xml` wire: an
# element whose text is empty or only whitespace has no `#text` for a field,
# but `when <path>/#text present` keeps its 0.5 meaning and holds when the
# element exists, whatever its text. Public. Two kinds: `t` when the element
# `v` exists, `other` (no `when`) for any other message. Each kind writes a
# constant attribute `k` naming it, so the output shows the kind selected.
# Unmapped child elements are not carried (ruling 6 of 0.1.1), and a `when
# ... present` writes nothing, so `v` is not written back.
format  conformance-transforms-xml-when
version 0.15.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses    probe
wire    xml
root    msg
kind    t
when    v/#text  present
requires probe.x
const   @k  t
field   probe.x  @x  iscale:1
kind    other
const   @k  other
field   probe.y  @y  int
